Tenaya ten (10) conduct Human Monk
Atheist, illiterate, vegan, vegetarian, weaponless, genoless,
polyselfless, polyitemless, wishless, artifact wishless

First of all, a big congratulations to Rachel E Dillon for her 10-
conduct monk ascension, in a streak, without startscumming, and having
the protection spell instead of sleeping.  I'll write about my
ascension but I'm somewhat embarrassed at the failures and methods of
my ascension although I am proud to have completed my project, learned
a lot about the game, and had fun.  Since we were playing a tournament
and I was running out of steam I resolved quite early to make use of a
known in-game abuse to identify the correct altar on the Astral
Plane.  It lessens my accomplishment but I'll try to redeem myself in
November.

At the end of May it came into my head to try to ascend a ten-conduct
monk with a starting spell of sleeping.  A monk seemed the natural
choice for vegan and vegetarian given the role intrinsics coupled with
a potion of acid for stoning emergencies, atheist took some
patience(and/or luck) related to finding holy water and caution
related to weak AC, illiteracy is not so bad with sleep being spammed
and caution related to weak AC, genoless is not that big a deal,
weaponless was accomplished by compulsively wielding nothing, hanging
out with a purple worm, being careful with my pick-axe (almost as
paranoid as with a rubber chicken) and not using a dagger to open
tins, wishless and polyless requires waiting for the RNG to be benign,
polyobjectless also meant that some Air Elementals on the Plane of Air
had a nice surprise coming.  Polyselfless was being appropriately
careful on DLVL 8 and below and lucky enough not to wander into a
trap.  I also made sure after wasting a charge in one of my games to
adjust the inventory letter of the Bell of Opening so that I wouldn't
accidentally apply it.  There is, after all, no way for an illiterate
atheist, wishless monk to recharge the Bell (without a lucky bones
file).

So after a few games, imagine my surprise when Shawn announced the
June NAO tournament!  Just days before the end of May I managed to
place an 8-conduct monk on the altar.  To make sure that I had the NAO
clock correct I waited to ascend until June 1 Universal Time.  I was a
little paranoid that I would start one hour early.  I truly thought
that I was ready for 10 conducts because my 8 conduct ascension was
only denied 9 conducts due to hitting a lichen with a dagger.  The
10th conduct, polyself, was lost due to an early polytrap.  The
attempt was educational because I found myself trapped in the wrong
high temple with insufficient means to cross back across the Astral
Plane.  Since I had already lost the polyself conduct, I changed into
a cockatrice corpse and made liberal use of the stoning grenades.  So,
I like to think that it could have been a 9-conduct ascension.  I
thought I was ready for the next step, but I was appropriately
humbled.

Here are some statistics:
80 games started
27 games starting with sleep spell and not quitscummed
5 lost polyself conduct due to 1 werejackal, 4 polytraps
2 lost due to despair from BOH accident and lightning
3 floating eyes (honestly, is dark blue a dev team trap?)
1 soldier with a wand of death
1 chickatrice, had a potion of acid in bag but did not retrieve in
time due to brain malfunction
3 big monster YASD (ouch minotaurs, trolls and dragons can hit hard
with AC =0)
10 small monster YASD (a small mimic! time to get some sleep)
1 eight conduct ascension
1 ten conduct ascension

Most of my losses in this project were the result of polyselfless
conduct loss, stupidity and sometimes a hostile/mischievious RNG.
Because I was playing exclusively for a 10-conduct ascension, stepping
on a polytrap was an insta-quit.

Some notable operator errors were:
~Escape keying through messages and not realizing that I was feverish
from a werejackal when I had wolfsbane in my inventory.
~Trying to save food and removing my amulet of reflection in the
castle, I think that I deserved the bolt of lightning that destroyed
my ring of conflict and slow digestion,
~n1000s'ing on the castle level and being unprepared to deal with the
Titan summoning storms
~trying to put scrolls into my bag of holding but accidentally
pressing "."  The subsequent despair resulted in feeding myself to a
minotaur.

The general scheme for each of my attempts was to first check my
starting spell and quitting if I had protection or healing.  Each game
was a race to start, as the plan was to complete the following tasks
prior to expiration of my sleep spell (turn 20,000):
1)	sleep spam my way to Sokoban gaining as much exp as possible,
2)	hope for the Bag of Holding
3)	find a ring of levitation, teleport, and teleport control
4)	get to XL 14
5)	go on quest
6)	kill Master Kaen
All of the above had to be accomplished without falling prey to a
polytrap, too.  The winning game turned out to have a level 3 jewelry
shop that I think helped in acquiring my Master Kaen ring set.  I also
found two bones files from the same player, both with valkyries and
with a wand of cancellation acquired my first holy water.

My usual method for gaining experience was succubus dancing and ghost
grinding.  For ghosts, I would dig a pit around the Minetown priest
and hit him with rocks just out of insect range.  Once dead I would
kill ghosts until 20,000 xp or 10,000 if succubi seemed in sufficient
supply.  I wouldn't usually kill the Quest home ghosts because going
all the way up to XL=14 takes too many ghosts so I had to have at
least one educational succubus experience.

Master Kaen, was always a challenge when I got to him.  He had an
uncanny ability to dodge sleeping spells even when already frozen.
The basic plan for him was:
1)	take off shoes
2)	put on rings of teleport and teleport control
3)	zap a wand of digging down (just for the off chance that I might
appear farther away from his starting position or next to lava)
4)	Put on boots of levitation
5)	Teleport next to lava
6)	Levitate over lava
7)	Quaff healing potions
8)	Zap MK with sleep
9)	Hit MK
10)	Repeat 7, 8 and 9 as necessary.
It was always high stress since MK can hit so hard and on one occasion
lost 100 hp from one attack! Ouch!  But once I had the Eyes of the
Overworld I was suddenly safe from polytraps and life got so much
easier because I was no longer racing the clock.

The 8-conduct ascension that I mentioned earlier taught me two things
in particular: using the amulet for portal detection is potentially
hazardous, and not having teleport zaps is potentially fatal.  So I
resolved to do a better job of glass orb and teleport wand acquisition
in this game.  I lack the patience to pudding farm so I grinded quest
home monsters for death drop loot.  I simply waited to the left of the
building and let earth elementals and xorns come towards me.  Early
on, I found a nurse who gave me almost 100 hp (yay! for no-teleport).
The xorns tended to drop pretty good items including an almost brand
new wand of teleport and a crystal ball.  Since it was no-teleport,
the xorn couldn't use the wand to flee and only got one zap from it
before I got him.  I also found a lot of wands of digging this way.
Although this generated a fair amount of potions and wands, it was no
substitute for randomly generated objects in the dungeon.

With 10 conducts one really has to make good use of what they find.
Losing rings to a blast of lightning could potentially mean having to
wait tens of thousands of turns for a ring death drop once the dungeon
has been cleared.  Also a bag of holding accident led to suicide,
too.  Basically I felt that I needed all of the loot in the dungeon
plus a little bit in order to survive.  Realizing this I needed to
find a way to gather a bunch of loot so I tried a couple of tactics
that didn't work well:
1)	waiting on the Elbereth in Sokoban (not good as too exposed)
2)	waiting on the Elbereth in the Castle (bad decision given the
caliber of the randomly generated monsters)

Another trick that I like doing is setting up Level 1 like a ranch and
waiting for cockatrice generation.  I thought that I had sufficient
cockatrices to give me a corpse to wield on Astral but the 3 or 4 that
I killed did not leave corpses.  It was a moot point anyway given that
I had a high level purple worm.

Before I cleared the Valley of the Dead, I spent some time with a
polytrap working on getting a couple of purple worms.  This is one of
my favorite game tricks.  I think I had four in this particular game,
2 were lost quite early but the second pair I used to clear the Valley
of the Dead.  Not only does this level the worms up to gargantuan
proportions but all of the loot carried but the undead is preserved
yielding handy wands and potions.  Sadly Big Purp ate a green slime
while I was looking for the vibrating square; I probably could have
displaced and taken the sliming instead of losing the worm but I
didn't think it through.  Big Dub was better taken care of and I even
ascended with him despite his eating a Rider wherein he vomited, died
and was revived with a wand of undead turning.  The Wizard of Yendor
was worm food and never presented a threat despite multiple
appearances.  It's amazing how powerful a level 45 purple worm is!  It
was a little silly in the end because I wasn't sure if he would ascend
with me if he was eating, but Death had caught up to me by the time I
reached the altar.  So, I had to keep jumping around trying to keep
Big Dub away from Death (to avoid a repeat Deathly meal) until I could
finally be on the altar with Big Dub next to me, and not eating, and
all at the same time.

Another challenging task was finding holy water since bones files
tended to have unholy water and without my starting holy water I did
not feel confident descending into Gehennom where my Bag of Holding
could potentially be cursed.  In some games I would get lucky and find
a bottle lying around and pet-test/name/#dip my various waters to
determine their B/U/C status.  Once I had my first holy water I had to
make sure that it didn't get boiled.  If I didn't find holy water on
the ground I had to hope for a Bones file with holy water in a bag
since open inventory waters were invariably cursed.  It seems trivial
now, but this was a big issue in most of my games.  Also, I needed
holy water in order to bless my bag of holding as inventory management
was a challenge during my race to Master Kaen.

For those of you with extra time on your hands here are the ttyrecs
for the whole game.  I watched a couple but was pretty bored.
Probably the only really interesting parts might be the first 20k
turns wherein I survived to Sokoban and then killed Master Kaen, and
perhaps the Ascension Run with my worm eating Rodney.  (Thanks to
rpresser for identifying the correct ttyrecs!)
